{# Web fonts, self-hosted (2026-10-29 speed pass). Replaces the per-page
   Google Fonts <link> in every _pageassets/<slug>-head.html, which cost each
   visit a render-blocking stylesheet from fonts.googleapis.com plus a second
   connection to fonts.gstatic.com before any text could be drawn in its font.

   The files in /fonts are Google's own woff2 files (same binaries the old
   links served; fetched from the css2 API on 2026-10-29, version in each
   filename), kept for the latin, latin-ext and greek subsets. The site uses
   Greek letters in its maths (Δ Σ β θ σ); cyrillic and vietnamese were never
   needed. A browser downloads a file only when a page draws a character in
   that face's unicode-range, so the unused faces cost nothing but the bytes
   of these rules.

   Each family is declared once with its full weight range, the union of what
   any page asked Google for, so every page gets the same faces. Licences:
   /fonts/licenses (SIL OFL 1.1). Filenames carry the upstream version, so
   _headers can mark /fonts/* immutable; a new version is a new filename.

   Preloaded: Inter regular (body text on every page) and Cormorant Garamond
   regular (page titles), latin subset only. Preload nothing else: every
   preload competes with the HTML's own critical resources.

   Do NOT add a fonts.googleapis.com link to a head fragment; the build lint in
   .eleventy.js fails on one. A new family or weight: fetch its woff2 the same
   way, add the rule here, see SITE_GUIDE "Web fonts". #}
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/inter-v20-normal-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/cormorant-garamond-v21-normal-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
